{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"7acdf6d3\" lines=\"25-42\">\n<description>\nMove the source-color pixels into the unique outline interior whose size matches the source count.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background and exactly two foreground colors.\n- One foreground color forms 8-connected outline objects with row-wise interior cells.\n- The other foreground color supplies a set of source pixels away from the chosen outline.\nRule\n- For each possible outline color, compute each 8-connected outline object's\n  row-span interior: background pixels strictly between the leftmost and\n  rightmost outline pixels on each occupied row.\n- Select the unique outline interior whose cell count equals the total\n  number of pixels of the other foreground color.\n- Erase the source pixels and paint that matched interior with the source color.\nKey insight\n- The colors are roles, not fixed IDs: the source color is identified by\n  counting, and the destination is the outline with a matching interior area.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e4941b18\" lines=\"8-22\">\n<description>\nMove red into teal's top marker position, then move teal to the bottom outside corner of the grey rectangle.\n\nInput structure\n- The dominant background surrounds one filled rectangular non-background block.\n- There is exactly one red marker and one teal marker, both in the row immediately above the rectangle.\n- Both markers are horizontally aligned over columns inside the rectangle.\n\nRule\n- Clear the original red marker.\n- Recolor the original teal marker cell red.\n- Place the teal marker beside the rectangle's bottom row, on the side indicated by the horizontal direction from red to teal.\n\nKey insight\n- The red-to-teal horizontal order chooses the rectangle side where teal exits at the bottom.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d6e50e54\" lines=\"8-25\">\n<description>\nMove each maroon marker toward the blue rectangle and recolor the rectangle red.\n\nInput structure\nA background canvas contains one solid blue rectangular object and several isolated\nmaroon marker pixels. Each marker is horizontally or vertically aligned with the\nrectangle and lies outside it.\n\nRule\nStart with a background canvas, repaint the blue rectangle red, and move each\nmaroon marker straight toward the rectangle along its row or column. Exactly one\nmarker is strictly closer to the rectangle than all others and enters the\nrectangle boundary; every other marker lands in the adjacent exterior cell just\noutside its aligned side.\n\nKey insight\nThe single entering marker is the unique global nearest marker to the rectangle,\nnot the nearest marker on each of the four sides.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"35ab12c3\" lines=\"73-88\">\n<description>\nComplete outlined shapes and carry attached shadow pixels along their edges.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. Each active color marks vertices of an 8-direction aligned outline.\n- A start vertex can have adjacent non-bg, different-colored shadow pixels.\n- Other colored pixels may be distractors unless they lie on valid drawable edges.\n\nRule:\n- For each color, order its pixels by polar angle around their centroid to form a cycle.\n- Draw only horizontal, vertical, or 45-degree edges whose interiors are clear.\n- From the chosen start vertex, copy adjacent shadow offsets along each drawable edge\n  when the parallel path is in bounds and clear.\n\nKey insight: The main outline is reconstructed first, then the start vertex's neighbor offsets define parallel shadow strokes.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"291dc1e1\" lines=\"7-22\">\n<description>\nReorder and stack rectangles by proximity to two colored edge lines.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Two edge lines (h + v) meet at a corner marked by a unique color.\n- \"Blue\" line is color 1 if present, else the longer line; other is \"red.\"\n- Solid rectangles in the interior.\n\nRule:\n- Sort rectangles by (distance to blue edge, distance to red edge).\n- If the blue edge is vertical, rotate each rectangle 90° CCW.\n- Stack top-to-bottom, centered horizontally.\n\nKey insight: Edge-line colors encode a coordinate system; proximity to each axis determines stacking order and rotation.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"edcc2ff0\" lines=\"47-63\">\n<description>\nKeep only the lower-panel colors named by the top markers and expand each marker into an object-count bar.\n\nInput structure\nA black instruction strip sits above a non-black rectangular scene panel.  The strip contains one-cell markers\nin the first column, and each marker color is a candidate object color in the lower panel.  The lower panel has\na unique dominant background color and scattered 4-connected foreground objects.\n\nRule\nIn the lower panel, preserve objects whose colors appear as top markers and recolor every other foreground\nobject to the panel background.  In the instruction strip, replace each marker by a horizontal run from column 0\nwhose length is the number of 4-connected lower-panel objects of that marker color; erase markers with count 0.\n\nKey insight\nThe top strip is a color filter plus a compact count summary: marker colors select which lower-panel objects\nsurvive, and their bars report the number of surviving objects by color.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"80a900e0\" lines=\"69-82\">\n<description>\nExtend diagonal rays outward from outer-border segments adjacent to diamond shapes on a checkerboard.\n\nInput structure:\n- Checkerboard bg (two most common colors).\n- Hollow diamond outlines (8-pixel) in a non-bg color (inner border).\n- Short diagonal line segments in another non-bg color adjacent to each diamond edge (outer border).\n\nRule:\n- For each outer-border segment, determine the outward direction (perpendicular to the segment, away from the diamond).\n- From each endpoint of the segment, cast a diagonal ray outward, painting over bg pixels with the segment's color until hitting a non-bg pixel or the grid edge.\n\nKey insight: Rays emit only from the two endpoints of each outer-border segment, not every pixel, and travel diagonally away from the diamond.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f1bcbc2c\" lines=\"40-55\">\n<description>\nPaint the top-connected middle channel between two orange path components teal.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is black.\n- One foreground color forms exactly two 4-connected one-pixel-wide path components.\n- Optional non-background control pixels may sit in the channel between the two paths.\n\nRule\n- Dilate each path component by one cell in the 8-neighborhood and intersect the two dilations; this gives the one-cell-wide middle channel.\n- A control pixel in that channel is a blocker only when its 4-neighbors touch fewer than both path components; otherwise it is part of the channel and is repainted.\n- After removing blockers, paint the channel component connected to the top edge teal and keep all other pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The desired pixels are not found by region filling; they are the geometric overlap of the two paths' one-cell halos, with weakly attached control pixels splitting the channel.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"52364a65\" lines=\"10-24\">\n<description>\nErase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\n\nInput structure:\n- A grid has one dominant background color and several monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects.\n- Each foreground object spans at least two columns in its bounding box.\n\nRule:\n- Find each same-color 4-connected foreground object.\n- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The deletion is measured from each object's local left edge, not from the grid edge or from a shared global column.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2de01db2\" lines=\"28-41\">\n<description>\nInvert each row's native foreground color against the black background.\n\nInput structure\n- A black-background grid whose rows each have one native foreground color plus optional distractor colors.\n- The native row color is the most frequent non-bg color in that row; if tied, its run starts leftmost among tied colors.\n\nRule\n- For each row independently, turn pixels of the native row color into bg.\n- Turn every other pixel in that row, including bg and distractor colors, into the native row color.\n\nKey insight\n- Distractor colors are not preserved objects; they mark cells that participate in the binary complement of the row's native color.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"da6e95e5\" lines=\"70-81\">\n<description>\nExtract the central object from the marker cluster whose markers have the same color.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background and several clusters; each cluster has four\nsame-color corner marker objects around one central monochromatic object.\nRule\nFind every central object enclosed by four aligned corner markers of one color,\nthen choose the unique one whose object color equals the marker color.\nKey insight\nThe answer is not the largest or most frequent object; it is the center of the\nself-colored cluster, cropped to that object's bounding box with background kept.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"98c475bf\" lines=\"62-76\">\n<description>\nErase the complete interior glyph and expand each endpoint marker pair into its color's full glyph.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid is 20x20 with background inside two same-color full-height vertical frame bars.\n- Inside the frame there is one complete color glyph and one or more other colors appearing only as two endpoint markers in the same row.\n- Marker endpoints are always in the first and last interior columns.\n\nRule\n- Keep the vertical frame unchanged.\n- Erase any complete interior glyph.\n- For each endpoint marker pair, use that marker color's learned glyph template and anchor its horizontal bar on the marker row.\n\nKey insight\n- Color identifies which glyph shape to draw; the two endpoint pixels are not copied objects, they are anchors for reconstructing that color's full symbol.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2ba387bc\" lines=\"6-21\">\n<description>\nSort scattered 4×4 squares into two columns by type: frames left, solids right.\n\nInput structure:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/9/des.md\"","aggregated_output":"<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据框架内部被遮挡的颜色层叠顺序，将各色框架拆分并按从内到外的顺序水平排列。\n- `Input structure`：背景色网格上有若干单像素厚的彩色矩形框架相互嵌套且部分重叠。每个框架使用不同颜色。框架之间存在交叉遮挡——在两个框架的边重合处，上层颜色覆盖下层颜色。此外，网格底部有一行标记带，其中包含若干单像素色块，颜色与部分框架颜色相同。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：通过框架交叉处的遮挡关系（哪个颜色覆盖了哪个颜色）推断出从最内层到最外层的完整嵌套顺序。\n  - 第二步：底部标记带中出现的颜色标记了需要保留的框架；未被标记的框架颜色在输出中被丢弃。\n  - 第三步：将保留的框架按嵌套顺序（最内层在左）从左到右水平排列在输出网格中，每个框架之间留一列背景色间隔。每个框架恢复为其完整的矩形轮廓（修复被遮挡的部分），大小保持原样。\n- `Key insight`：遮挡关系不是简单的\"谁在上面\"，而是编码了嵌套深度；底部标记带起到筛选作用，两层推理缺一不可——先从交叉点归纳嵌套序，再用标记带过滤。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将散落的彩色碎片拼入唯一与其轮廓互补的模板孔洞中，碎片需要旋转到正确朝向。\n- `Input structure`：背景色网格被一列灰色分隔线分为左右两个面板。左面板包含若干不同颜色的实心模板形状，每个模板内部有一个由背景色构成的孔洞（形状各异）。右面板散落着若干彩色小碎片（每个碎片是一个 4-连通的单色小形状），碎片颜色各不相同且与模板颜色不同。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对于右面板中的每个碎片，尝试将其旋转 0°、90°、180°、270° 四种朝向。\n  - 将旋转后的碎片形状与左面板中每个模板的孔洞形状进行匹配——匹配条件是碎片像素集合与孔洞像素集合完全重合。\n  - 每个碎片恰好匹配唯一一个模板孔洞和唯一一个旋转角度。\n  - 在输出中，将碎片以匹配的旋转角度填入对应模板的孔洞位置，碎片保持自身颜色；右面板中该碎片的原始位置清除为背景色。\n- `Key insight`：解题者不能仅凭碎片面积匹配孔洞——必须在四种旋转中找到精确的形状吻合；旋转角度的确定是隐蔽的核心推理步骤。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据每个封闭区域内标记像素的颜色，用该颜色重新绘制区域的边界线段。\n- `Input structure`：背景色网格上有一个由灰色线段构成的不规则网络，这些线段将网格分割成若干封闭区域（每个区域是一个由灰色边界围成的 4-连通背景色区域）。部分封闭区域内包含恰好一个非灰色、非背景色的单像素标记点，标记点颜色各不相同。部分区域没有标记点。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：识别灰色线段网络划分出的所有封闭区域。\n  - 第二步：对于每个包含标记点的区域，找到该区域的所有边界灰色像素（即与该区域的背景像素 4-邻接的灰色像素）。\n  - 第三步：如果一个灰色边界像素仅与一个含标记区域相邻，则将其重新着色为该标记的颜色。如果一个灰色边界像素同时与两个含标记区域相邻，则保持灰色不变（共享墙壁保留原色）。\n  - 第四步：不含标记的区域的专属边界（不与任何含标记区域共享的灰色像素）也保持灰色不变。标记点本身在输出中被清除为背景色。\n- `Key insight`：关键不在于\"找到标记点\"这一步，而在于理解边界像素的归属规则——共享墙壁不被染色，只有专属于单个标记区域的边界才变色。解题者需要从样例中归纳出这条共享墙壁例外规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：沿着每个箭头指示的方向，将箭头所在对象的副本逐步印章式复制，直到碰到另一个对象或网格边缘，最终移除所有箭头标记。\n- `Input structure`：背景色网格上有若干不同颜色的 4-连通实心对象（形状各异，大小约 3×3 到 5×5）。每个对象的边缘恰好有一个单像素的特殊标记色（maroon）像素，该 maroon 像素替换了对象边缘的一个像素位置。maroon 像素相对于对象质心的方向指示了该对象的\"投射方向\"（上、下、左、右四个正方向之一，由 maroon 像素位于对象边界的哪一侧决定：位于对象最上行则方向为上，位于最下行则方向为下，位于最左列则方向为左，位于最右列则方向为右）。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：识别每个对象及其 maroon 标记像素的位置，确定投射方向。\n  - 第二步：将 maroon 像素恢复为该对象自身的颜色（修复对象）。\n  - 第三步：沿投射方向，以对象包围盒大小为步长，逐步复制该对象的完整形状。每次复制的位置紧接上一个副本。如果下一个副本的任何像素会落在非背景色像素上或超出网格边界，则停止复制。\n  - 第四步：所有副本使用原对象的颜色绘制。原始对象保留在原位。\n- `Key insight`：解题者首先需要识别 maroon 像素不是独立标记，而是嵌在对象边缘的方向指针；然后需要归纳出\"沿指向方向等距印章复制直到碰撞\"的规则。方向的判定（maroon 在对象包围盒的哪一侧边缘）是隐蔽的第一层推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：通过比较同色对象对的形状差异，找到缺失的像素位置，并用另一种颜色在该位置标记。\n- `Input structure`：背景色网格上有若干彩色 4-连通对象。这些对象按颜色配对——每种前景色恰好出现两个对象。同色的两个对象形状几乎相同，但其中一个比另一个多出恰好一个像素（即较大者是较小者加上一个额外像素）。网格角落有一个单独的 red 像素作为全局标记。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：按颜色将对象配对。对于每对同色对象，将两者的包围盒对齐（左上角重合），然后找出较大对象相比较小对象多出的那一个像素的相对位置。\n  - 第二步：将该多出像素在较大对象中的绝对网格坐标记录下来。\n  - 第三步：在输出中，所有原始对象保持不变，但在每个多出像素的位置上方（上一行、同一列）放置一个 red 像素。如果上方位置已有非背景像素或超出网格，则放在下方。\n  - 第四步：移除角落的全局 red 标记。\n- `Key insight`：核心在于解题者必须发现\"同色配对 → 形状对比 → 差异定位\"这条推理链。仅凭单个对象无法确定标记位置，必须通过两个几乎相同对象的比较来揭示差异像素；red 标记色的角色需从角落提示中归纳。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据各色路径穿过色带的顺序，对路径重新着色。\n- `Input structure`：背景色网格上有若干条水平色带（每条色带占一行，颜色各不相同，横跨网格全宽）。色带之间被背景行隔开。网格上还有若干条灰色的竖直路径（每条路径宽一像素，从网格顶部延伸到底部），这些路径穿过所有色带。每条灰色路径在某些色带行会产生交叉点。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：识别所有竖直灰色路径和所有水平色带。\n  - 第二步：对于每条灰色路径，记录它从上到下依次穿过的色带颜色序列。\n  - 第三步：该路径的输出颜色由它穿过的第一条（最上方的）色带的颜色决定。将整条路径（包括穿过色带的交叉点）重新着色为该颜色。\n  - 第四步：色带本身保持不变。如果路径的新颜色与其穿过的某条色带颜色相同，则在该交叉点处路径颜色优先显示。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先识别出\"色带\"和\"路径\"是两种不同的结构元素，然后发现路径颜色由其穿过的第一条色带决定——而不是由最后一条、最多的一条或路径本身的位置决定。色带的排列顺序本身是一种编码系统。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中的多个小图案按照它们与边框连接线的拓扑关系重新排列到指定的输出槽位中。\n- `Input structure`：背景色网格的四条边上各有若干个单像素的彩色锚点（颜色各不相同）。从每个锚点出发，有一条同色的单像素宽线段向网格内部延伸（水平或竖直方向），线段末端连接着一个灰色的小矩形区域（约 3×3 到 5×5）。每个灰色矩形内部包含一个由非灰色、非背景色像素构成的独特小图案。网格中央有一个由灰色边框围成的大矩形输出区域，该区域内部被灰色线分割成若干个与小矩形等大的槽位。每个槽位的边缘有一个单像素彩色标记，颜色与某个边框锚点颜色对应。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：识别边框上的每个彩色锚点，沿其连接线找到对应的灰色小矩形，提取其中的小图案。\n  - 第二步：在中央输出区域中，找到带有相同颜色标记的槽位。\n  - 第三步：将提取的小图案放入对应颜色标记的槽位中。图案在槽位中居中放置，保持原始朝向。\n  - 第四步：移除所有连接线和边框锚点，仅保留中央输出区域及其中填好的图案。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要建立\"边框锚点颜色 → 连接线 → 源图案\"和\"槽位颜色标记 → 目标位置\"两条映射链，然后通过颜色匹配将两条链关联起来。颜色在这里不是装饰属性，而是路由地址。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据每个对象被网格线切割后产生的碎片数目，决定该对象在输出中的存留或删除。\n- `Input structure`：背景色网格上有一组均匀分布的细虚线网格线（由间隔排列的灰色像素构成，水平和竖直各若干条），将网格划分成若干等大的格子。网格上还有若干个不同颜色的 4-连通实心对象，这些对象跨越多个格子，被虚线网格线切割。在网格的一个角落有一个小的\"图例区\"——一个由灰色边框围成的小方格，内部显示一个数字状的像素图案，表示阈值数 T（T 的值为 2 或 3，用像素点阵的方式画出）。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：识别虚线网格线将每个对象切割成的连通碎片数量（沿网格线将对象像素擦除后，统计剩余像素的 4-连通分量数）。\n  - 第二步：读取角落图例中的阈值数 T。\n  - 第三步：如果一个对象被切割成的碎片数量严格大于 T，则在输出中保留该对象（恢复被网格线擦除的像素，即完整显示该对象）。如果碎片数量小于或等于 T，则将该对象完全删除（替换为背景色）。\n  - 第四步：虚线网格线在输出中全部移除。角落图例也移除。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现虚线网格线的\"切割\"作用——它们不是装饰，而是将对象拆分成碎片的工具；然后需要归纳出\"碎片数与阈值比较\"这一筛选规则。两层推理都非显然：第一层需要理解网格线的功能含义，第二层需要从样例中归纳出阈值比较的方向（大于而非小于）。\n</new_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"建模方案已经确定：\n\n1. 求解器把“灰线”视为唯一墙色，先找所有 `非墙色` 的 4 连通分量；不触边的分量就是封闭区域。\n2. 每个封闭区域里至多有一个非背景标记色。对每个含标记区域，只从该区域的背景像素出发收集相邻灰墙，统计每个灰墙像素挨着几个“含标记区域”。\n3. 只挨着 1 个含标记区域的墙像素重染成该标记色；同时挨着 2 个含标记区域的共享墙保持灰色；标记点本身清回背景。\n\n生成器我会用“外框 + 粗网格分区”的方式做：\n1. 先把画布切成 3x3 到 4x4 的大单元，每个单元尺寸随机。\n2. 在粗网格上随机合并相邻单元形成不规则区域，再栅格化成 1 像素厚灰墙网络。\n3. 强制样例同时包含：至少两个相邻的含标记区域、至少一个无标记区域、至少一段会被染色的专属墙、至少一段保持灰色的共享墙。\n4. 最后用 `main()` 回验生成样例，确保生成器和规则完全一致。"}}
